<!-- WEBWORK_FLORA_ROSTER_1 build. Authority:
     design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_flora_roster_2026-09-23.md — 16
     RM_-tier invented plants organised in four registers (the thicket, the
     plumbing, the nightmare plants, the white half and the margin). These
     replace the vanilla-Core placeholder wildPlants (Plant_TreeOak/
     Plant_TreePoplar/Plant_Bush/Plant_TallGrass/Plant_Berry) that
     WEBWORK_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 shipped on RM_Webwork_Biome.xml as an interim
     "loads on Core alone" filler, per that item's own comment naming this
     roster item as the follow-on that supplies the real cast.

     🔴 The 7 donor rows this roster's own §7 disposes of
     (AB_JungleTree/RG_Plant_TropicalChokevine/AB_TangleTea/AB_Gomphoeria/
     AB_RedBugloss/AB_Aaklac cut; Plant_TookeTrap_Wild moved to the Utinni
     layer, sitting record §6 rulings 8/9) live ONLY on the FROZEN
     `RUT_Webwork.xml` twin, which this build does not touch (Phase A rule:
     the frozen def is carried byte-for-byte until the terminal paint). They
     were never copied into RM_Webwork, so there is nothing to physically cut
     here — the disposition is satisfied by RM_Webwork simply never carrying
     them and by `Plant_TookeTrap_Wild` arriving only through
     UtinniPatches/Patches/WildPlants_Webwork.xml below.

     No new C# — every mechanism the roster names (churn engine, snap-trigger,
     needle-cast, scent-lure, front-creep, fresh/withered route-state) is
     flagged OWED by the roster doc itself; these are plain wildPlants rows
     wired to existing shipped systems where one already exists
     (RM_MapComponent_FrontCreep for grennick's context) and otherwise scoped
     as future build work, same precedent as FEVERWOOD_FLORA_ROSTER_1.

     ART: infrastructure/artpipe/registry.jsonl, done/, _artsrc/ and pending/
     were searched for all 16 names before this build — zero hits (MEASURED,
     sanity-probed against korrum/stoneback/hawkbat which all returned real
     counts). Every row below ships a flat-color placeholder PNG (same idiom
     as RM_FeverWoodFlora.xml's placeholders: a filled ellipse + dark outline
     on a transparent 256x256 canvas) and a fresh artpipe queue entry
     (infrastructure/artpipe/pending/webwork_plant_<name>.json,
     rimflow_item_id=WEBWORK_FLORA_ROSTER_1). -->
<Defs>

  <!-- ===================== THE THICKET — the green half (5 rows) ===================== -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RM_Kollavane</defName>
    <label>kollavane</label>
    <description>Not one tree but a standing braid of dozens — pale green whips fused into a dark trunk, new shoots erupting from the base while the crown's older wood dies black. It is visibly several ages at once. The thicket's body: the young whip-masses are what the nest is woven from, and its churn-dead wood is the biome's only timber — nobody fells a living one, they salvage what the braid discarded.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>150</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.3</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Kollavane/RM_Kollavane_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.3, 0.5, 0.3)</volume>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>40</pathCost>
    <plant>
      <fertilityMin>0.4</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0.3</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>35</growDays>
      <dieIfLeafless>false</dieIfLeafless>
