    <label>varrisk</label>
    <description>A dull green sedge standing in oddly even stands — spaced, aligned, unmistakably planted rather than grown. Dry-country foliage, waxed against the heat. The reach: the irrigated lowland cover at the end of the plumbing. Where varrisk stands, silk water reaches; where it stops, the desert has won.</description>
